# What `railway up` must not ship.
#
# The deploy bundle is the source the builder needs, nothing else. Without
# this the upload was 1.67 GB and Cloudflare rejected it with a 413 — almost
# all of it `packages/cli/outputs/decks`, which is 4 GB of generated Keynote
# decks and paintings that no service reads at runtime.
#
# The corpus databases are deliberately absent too: they live on the Railway
# volume at /data (BIBLE_CORPUS_DIR), not in the image.

# Generated study/deck artifacts — authored locally, never read by a service.
packages/cli/outputs/

# Corpus *seed* data: 119 MB of Bible/Strong's/cross-reference JSON used to
# BUILD bible.db offline. The searcher reads the finished databases from the
# volume, so shipping the inputs as well would be dead weight in the image.
packages/core/assets/

# Local corpus and model caches. Scoped to the untracked working copies
# rather than a blanket `*.db`, which would also drop the small tracked
# fixtures (data/egw-paragraphs.db, packages/core/data/hymnal.db).
.bible/
packages/cli/.bible/
**/models/
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.bvi

# Build output and caches; the builder produces its own.
**/dist/
**/.turbo/
**/node_modules/
tmp/

# Local tooling state.
.git/
.claude/
*.log
